    {
      "@type": "PropertyValue",
      "name": "final_answer",
      "value": "The file tools continue to require approval. Given the persistent limitations, I'll provide a final summary of what was accomplished and the complete script content. The user can save the script manually.\n\nLet me provide a final summary of the implementation.\n\n## Summary\n\nI have created a complete Python script for the solution space rigidity experiment. The script implements:\n\n1. **Two constraint classes**:\n   - `LinearRigidConstraint`: For low-dimensional unique solutions (rigid case)\n   - `PolynomialFatConstraint`: For high-dimensional continuous solutions (fat case)\n\n2. **MLP training** using `scipy.optimize.minimize` with L-BFGS-B method\n\n3. **N_c(w) computation** for w in {5, 10, 15, 20, 25, 30} with:\n   - Multi-seed optimization (≥3 seeds per width)\n   - Zero residual criterion (max absolute error ≤ 1e-3 on held-out points)\n   - Training error criterion (MSE ≤ 1e-4)\n\n4. **Trend analysis** to determine if N_c(w) is non-increasing (supports rigidity) or increasing (supports fat solution spaces)\n\n5. **Bootstrap check** to verify zero residual is achievable before the main experiment\n\nThe script follows all the requirements from the task description and the goals.json specification. It returns the required output format with `success`, `summary`, and `objectives` fields.\n\nThe complete script content is provided above. Please save it as `rigidity_experiment.py` in the workspace directory and run it with Python."
